# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
obj/
publish/
*.pdb

# ── Personal settings & secrets: never commit these ───────────────────────────
# VME stores API keys (DPAPI-encrypted, but still personal) in config.json next
# to the EXE; keep any local copy out of the repo. Same for Subtitle Studio.
config.json
subt_settings.json
error.log
*.diag.txt

# ── Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code user files ────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs

# ── OS clutter ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# NOTE: do NOT add "native/" here. Git on Windows matches case-insensitively, so it
# would also hide the source folder VideoMetadataEditor/Native/. The runtime native\
# tools folder lives inside publish\, which is already ignored above.
